@@ -69,6 +69,17 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    >>> console.out("Hello", "World!", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+It does not pretty print containers, wrap or crop text, apply console markup, or replace emoji codes. Markup-like text and emoji codes are written literally. Output is still passed through the console's render hooks, and buffering and capture work as they do for print.
+
+By default ``out`` applies highlighting (``highlight=True``), even if the console has highlighting disabled. Pass ``highlight=None`` to use the console setting, or ``highlight=False`` to turn highlighting off. The ``style`` argument accepts a style name or a :class:`~rich.style.Style` object and is applied in the same way as print.
+
 
